Subject: [PATCH] djihads-gather-owners: gathered multi-range copies die with their sources (EDEN_UP_DJ_GATHER_OWNERS=1)

djihads-gather-owners: gathered multi-range copies die with their sources (EDEN_UP_DJ_GATHER_OWNERS=1)

Ported from Djihads80/Eglantine nx2-experimental c6d2acd37 ("nx2: Ocarina of Time stability,
shader and performance fixes", #794, "release gathered buffers together with their sources"),
GPL-3.0-or-later, vk_multi_range_buffer.cpp/.h and BufferCacheRuntime::TickFrame.
Co-authors per that commit.

A multi-range storage binding that can't be bound sparse is served by a gathered device-local
copy. Only sparse entries recorded their source buffers as owners, so deleting a source dropped
the sparse alias but never the gathered copy: it lived on until its key came back with another
layout (device memory held for buffers that are gone; on a reused VkBuffer handle the cached copy
can be taken for the new buffer's). With the switch every entry records its owners, DropOwner
retires gathered copies too, and the retired ones are freed each frame once the GPU is done with
them (TickFrame) instead of only on the next Get.
Off (unset): byte-identical (TickFrame returns at once). No new scheduler Wait/Finish site
(prepare-vulkan-port counts them).

Checks (djihads-c6d2_checks.sh, log djihads-c6d2.checks.log): git apply --check on the T82 core,
patch on a copy, prepare-vulkan-port.py same 6 anchor skips as baseline, -fsyntax-only rc=0 on
every TU the diff reaches (generated copies included), injected static_assert seen in each,
and all four djihads-*.diff stack in one tree (same anchors, rc=0). Not built, not run.

